On Sat, 1 Dec 2007, Ohle Claussen wrote:
> How is noting down every object identity (and subsequently looking them up
> again) easier than storing screenshots of levels?

It's rare that you'll get sucked before you notice an MF is on the level.
So you can hit "\" and copy everything down at the last minute.

There's no way in Nethack to access your in-game memory of other levels
without travelling to them, so if you want to save your maps you have to
maintain screenshotting discipline throughout the game.

(A TTY recording would make that effortless, but I think that scores
quite a lot higher on the cheat-o-meter than merely keeping out of game
notes.  And it could also be used to recover ID information.)

You can also easily re-insert saved ID information back into the game via
the #name feature, so long as you have example objects.  It's not possible
to re-insert map information.

